<title>VENEZUELA: Santander launches Venezuela equity basket warrant.</title>
<headline>Santander launches Venezuela equity basket warrant.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Santander de Negocios SA said it has  launched 750,000 European style call warrants on a basket of Venezuelan  equities.</p>
<p>Each basket is comprised of the following stocks:</p>
<p>CANTV 0.2292 shares</p>
<p>Electricidad de Caracas 4.5892 shares</p>
<p>Sivensa 8.9254 shares</p>
<p>Vencemos 1.1487 shares</p>
<p>One warrant controls one basket.</p>
<p>    STRIKE PRICE     $27.50    PREMIUM 29.90 PERCENT</p>
<p>    ISSUE PRICE	$4.975    GEARING 5.00x</p>
<p>    LISTING   LUXEMBOURG SE    MATURITY 28 JAN 1999</p>
<p>    PAYDATE     20 AUG 1997</p>
<p>The warrants are not being offered or sold in the United States or  to U.S. citizens.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
